{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-31-1","title":"Job 31:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job makes a solemn protestation of his integrity in several duties.</p>\n<p>a covenant. Ge 6:2; 2Sa 11:2-4; Ps 119:37; Pr 4:25; 23:31-33; Mt 5:28,29 1Jo 2:16 think. Pr 6:25; Jas 1:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-2","title":"Job 31:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>20:29; 27:13; Heb 13:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-3","title":"Job 31:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>destruction. 21:30; Ps 55:23; 73:18; Pr 1:27; 10:29; 21:15; Mt 7:13; Ro 9:22 1Th 5:3; 2Th 1:9; 2Pe 2:1 a strange. Isa 28:21; Jude 1:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-4","title":"Job 31:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>14:16; 34:21; Ge 16:13; 2Ch 16:9; Ps 44:21; 139:1-3; Pr 5:21; 15:3 Jer 16:17; 32:19; Joh 1:48; Heb 4:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-5","title":"Job 31:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>If. Ps 7:3-5 walked. Ps 4:2; 12:2; 44:20,21; Pr 12:11; Jer 2:5; Eze 13:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-6","title":"Job 31:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Let me be weighed in an even balance. Heb. Let him weigh mein balances of justice. 1Sa 2:3; Ps 7:8,9; 17:2,3; 26:1; Pr 16:11; Isa 26:7; Da 5:27 Mic 6:11 know. Jos 22:22; Ps 1:6; 139:23; Mt 7:23; 2Ti 2:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-7","title":"Job 31:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>If my. Ps 44:20,21 mine heart. Nu 15:39; Ec 11:9; Eze 6:9; 14:3,7; Mt 5:29 cleaved. Ps 101:3; Isa 33:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-8","title":"Job 31:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>let me. 5:5; 24:6; Le 26:16; De 28:30-33,38,51; Jud 6:3-6; Mic 6:15 let my. 5:4; 15:30; 18:19; Ps 109:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-9","title":"Job 31:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>If mine. Jud 16:5; 1Ki 11:4; Ne 13:26; Pr 2:16-19; 5:3-23; 6:25; 7:21; 22:14 Ec 7:26 if I. 24:15,16; Jer 5:8; Ho 7:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-10","title":"Job 31:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>grind. Ex 11:5; Isa 47:2; Mt 24:41 and let. 2Sa 12:11; Jer 8:10; Ho 4:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-11","title":"Job 31:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>an heinous. Ge 20:9; 26:10; 39:9; Ex 20:14; Pr 6:29-33 an iniquity. 28; Ge 38:24; Le 20:10; De 22:22-24; Eze 16:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-12","title":"Job 31:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Pr 3:33; 6:27; Jer 5:7-9; Mal 3:5; Heb 13:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-13","title":"Job 31:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>the cause. Ex 21:20,21,26,27; Le 25:43,46; De 15:12-15; Jer 34:14-17 Eph 6:9; Col 4:1 when.In ancient times slaves had no action at law against their owners; but Job admitted them to all civil rights, and permitted them to complain even against himself.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-14","title":"Job 31:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>What then. 9:32; 10:2; Ps 7:6; 9:12,19; 10:12-15; 44:21; 76:9; 143:2; Isa 10:3 Zec 2:13 when he. Ho 9:7; Mic 7:4; Mr 7:2; Jas 2:13 what shall. Ro 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-15","title":"Job 31:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Did not he. 34:19; Ne 5:5; Pr 14:31; 22:2; Isa 58:7; Mal 2:10 did not one fashion us in the womb? or, did he not fashionus in one womb? 10:8-12; Ps 139:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-16","title":"Job 31:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>withheld. 22:7-9; De 15:7-10; Ps 112:9; Lu 16:21; Ac 11:29; Ga 2:10 the eyes. De 28:32; Ps 69:3; 119:82,123; Isa 38:14; La 4:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-17","title":"Job 31:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>have. De 15:11,14; Ne 8:10; Lu 11:41; Joh 13:29; Ac 4:32 the fatherless. 29:13-16; Eze 18:7,16; Ro 12:13; Jas 1:27; 1Jo 3:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-18","title":"Job 31:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>her. that is, the widow.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-19","title":"Job 31:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>22:6; 2Ch 28:15; Isa 58:7; Mt 25:36,43; Lu 3:11; Ac 9:39; Jas 2:16 1Jo 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-20","title":"Job 31:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>29:11; De 24:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-21","title":"Job 31:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>lifted. 6:27; 22:9; 24:9; 29:12; Pr 23:10,11; Jer 5:28; Eze 22:7 when. Mic 2:1,2; 7:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-22","title":"Job 31:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>let. 10,40; Jos 22:22,23; Ps 7:4,5; 137:6 bone. or, chanel bone.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-23","title":"Job 31:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>destruction. 20:23; 21:20; Ge 39:9; Ps 119:120; Isa 13:6; Joe 1:15; 2Co 5:11 by. 13:11; 40:9; 42:5,6; Ps 76:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-24","title":"Job 31:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Ge 31:1; De 8:12-14; Ps 49:6,7,17; 52:7; 62:10; Pr 10:15; 11:28 Pr 30:9; Mr 10:24; Lu 12:15; Col 3:5; 1Ti 6:10,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-25","title":"Job 31:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>rejoiced. Es 5:11; Pr 23:5; Jer 9:23; Eze 28:5; Lu 12:19; 16:19,25 because. De 8:17,18; Isa 10:13,14; Da 4:30; Ho 12:8; Hab 1:16 gotten much. Heb. found much.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-26","title":"Job 31:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>beheld. Ge 1:16-18; De 4:19; 11:16; 17:3; 2Ki 23:5,11; Jer 8:2; Eze 8:16 sun. Heb. light. the moon. Ps 8:3,4; Jer 44:17 in brightness. Heb. bright.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-27","title":"Job 31:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>my heart. De 11:16; 13:6; Isa 44:20; Ro 1:21,28 my mouth hath kissed my hand. Heb. my hand hath kissed mymouth. 1Ki 19:18; Ps 2:12; Ho 13:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-28","title":"Job 31:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>an. 11; 9:15; 23:7; Ge 18:25; De 17:2-7,9; Jud 11:27; Ps 50:6; Heb 12:23 for. Jos 24:23,27; Pr 30:9; Tit 1:16; 2Pe 2:1; 1Jo 2:23; Jude 1:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-29","title":"Job 31:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>2Sa 1:12; 4:10,11; 16:5-8; Ps 35:13,14,25,26; Pr 17:5; 24:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-30","title":"Job 31:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>have. Ex 23:4,5; Mt 5:43,44; Ro 12:14; 1Pe 2:22,23; 3:9 mouth. Heb. palate. Ec 5:2,6; Mt 5:22; 12:36; Jas 3:6,9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-31","title":"Job 31:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>the men. 1Sa 24:4,10; 26:8; 2Sa 16:9,10; 19:21,22; Jer 40:15,16; Lu 9:54,55 Lu 22:50,51 Oh. 19:22; Ps 27:2; 35:25; Pr 1:11,12,18; Mic 3:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-32","title":"Job 31:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>The stranger. 17,18; Ge 19:2,3; Jud 19:15,20,21; Isa 58:7; Mt 25:35,40,44,45 Ro 12:13; 1Ti 5:10; Heb 13:2; 1Pe 4:9 traveller. or, way.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-33","title":"Job 31:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>covered. Ge 3:7,8,12; Jos 7:11; Pr 28:13; Ho 6:7; Ac 5:8; 1Jo 1:8-10 as Adam. or, after the manner of men. Ho 6:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-34","title":"Job 31:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Did I. Ex 23:2; Pr 29:25; Jer 38:4,5,16,19; Mt 27:20-26 the contempt. 22:8; 34:19; Ex 32:27; Nu 25:14,15; Ne 5:7; 13:4-8,28; 2Co 5:16 that I. Es 4:11,14; Pr 24:11,12; Am 5:11-13; Mic 7:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-35","title":"Job 31:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>Oh. 13:3; 17:3; 23:3-7; 33:6; 38:1-3; 40:4,5 my desire is, that the Almighty would answer me. or, my signis that the Almighty will answer me. 13:21,22; Ps 26:1 mine. 13:24; 19:11,23,24; 33:10,11; Mt 5:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-36","title":"Job 31:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>I. Ex 28:12; Isa 22:22 a crown. 29:14; Isa 62:3; Php 4:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-37","title":"Job 31:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>declare. 9:3; 13:15; 14:16; 42:3-6; Ps 19:12 as a. Ge 32:28; Eph 3:12; Heb 4:15,16; 1Jo 3:19-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-38","title":"Job 31:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>cry. 20:27; Hab 2:11; Jas 5:4 complain. Heb. weep. Ps 65:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-39","title":"Job 31:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>fruits. Heb. strength. Ge 4:12 caused the owners thereof to lose their life. Heb. causedthe soul of the owners thereof to expire, or breathe out. 1Ki 21:13-16,19; Pr 1:19; Isa 26:21; Eze 22:6,12,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-31-40","title":"Job 31:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>thistles.{Choach,} probably the black thorn. (See on 2 Ki 14:9.)</p>\n<p>Ge 3:17,18; Isa 7:23; Zep 2:9; Mal 1:3 cockle. or, noisome weeds. The. Ps 72:20</p>"}]}